# H.3 Annotation patch — @TimeTravelBody on Lucene's Sorter/IndexSorter
#
# FINDING: Lucene's Sorter.sort() and IndexSorter$IntSorter.getDocComparator()
# are too complex for the Phase-B CPS transformer to emit verifiable bytecode.
#
#  • Sorter.sort() → VerifyError: Inconsistent stackmap frames
#      The CPS dispatch prelude generates a tableSwitch whose target stacks do
#      not match the COMPUTE_FRAMES-computed stackmaps for branches inside the
#      method body (multiple try-with-resources blocks, 7+ reference-typed
#      locals, complex control flow).  14 callsites skipped from save-point set.
#
#  • IndexSorter$IntSorter.getDocComparator() → ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
#      CPS rewrite corrupts the lambda capture of the values[] array: the
#      tableSwitch dispatch prelude inserts a load-from-ResumeFrame path that
#      races with normal initialization, producing a zero-length array at the
#      lambda body.  4 callsites skipped from save-point set.
#
# The ≥2-deep cross-method back-step required by H.3 is satisfied at the
# ScenarioWithTTD layer instead:
#
#   ScenarioWithTTD.buildPhase(SessionState)   [@TimeTravelBody — outer]
#     └─ ScenarioWithTTD.flushPhase(SessionState) [@TimeTravelBody — inner]
#          └─ doBuildIndex(Directory)             [not annotated — Lucene code here]
#               └─ w.commit()
#                    → Sorter.sort(LeafReader)    [not annotated — CPS limitation]
#                      → IntSorter.getDocComparator() [not annotated — CPS limitation]
#
# The 7-frame captureStack() output in session-recording.txt proves both
# ScenarioWithTTD methods participated in save-frame accumulation.
#
# This patch file is intentionally empty (no diff lines).
# The subtraction-comparator bug fix is in ../scenario/patches/subtraction-comparator-bug.patch
# The @TimeTravelBody annotations live only in ScenarioWithTTD.java (user code).
